// Blocks ways that OSM's conditional tags close to pedestrians on the day the
// graph was built. Applied to foot, hike, stroller and easyhike.
//
// car_temporal.json carries the full explanation. The one judgement specific to
// this file: upstream suggests a hint rather than a block for foot, on the
// grounds that pedestrian conditionals are often minor. We block anyway, for
// consistency with the other two and because the alternative needs a path
// detail the web app would have to render -- and 11.0 has no
// `access_conditional` detail to render.
{
  "priority": [
    { "if": "foot_temporal_access == NO", "multiply_by": "0" }
  ]
}
